goav1
=====

Pure-Go AV1 implementation focused on realtime/WebRTC decoding.

This project ports behavior from a set of pinned upstream sources.
See third_party/upstream.lock for the exact pinned git object of
every upstream consulted while writing this code. Local working
clones of each upstream live under third_party/upstream/<name>/ and
are ignored by git but produced on demand by `make sync-upstreams`.

The list below covers the third-party projects whose code, behavior,
or specifications this repository derives from. Each upstream is
distributed under its own license; the local checkout preserves the
upstream LICENSE / COPYING / PATENTS files verbatim.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. libaom (AV1 reference encoder/decoder)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:   https://aomedia.googlesource.com/aom
Pinned tag: v3.14.0
Pinned at:  third_party/upstream/libaom/ (sync via `make sync-upstreams`)
License:    BSD 2-Clause + Alliance for Open Media Patent License 1.0
Files:      third_party/upstream/libaom/LICENSE
            third_party/upstream/libaom/PATENTS

Copyright notice (verbatim from libaom LICENSE):

    Copyright (c) 2016, Alliance for Open Media. All rights reserved.

A copy of the libaom BSD 2-Clause license is reproduced as the goav1
root LICENSE file. The Alliance for Open Media Patent License 1.0 is
reproduced verbatim as the goav1 root PATENTS file, satisfying the
"reproduce this License with any Implementation" condition in section
1.2.1 of that grant.

Files in this repository whose logic is derived from libaom should
cite their upstream source path with a comment of the form

    // Ported from libaom: av1/<path>.c

near the top of the file or function. Direct numerical tables (CDF
defaults, dequantization scales, transform scan orders, qmatrix
levels, etc.) are reproduced as published in libaom.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. dav1d (VideoLAN AV1 decoder)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:   https://code.videolan.org/videolan/dav1d.git
Pinned tag: 1.5.3
Pinned at:  third_party/upstream/dav1d/ (sync via `make sync-upstreams`)
License:    BSD 2-Clause
File:       third_party/upstream/dav1d/COPYING

Copyright notice (verbatim from dav1d COPYING):

    Copyright (c) 2018-2025, VideoLAN and dav1d authors
    All rights reserved.

dav1d is consulted as a reference for decoder architecture, OBU
parsing layout, tile/decode pipeline shape, and DSP organization.
Several internal Go packages are structurally inspired by its layout.
The raw ARM64 instructions in
internal/av1/decoder/loop_filter_sb_neon_arm64.s are adapted from
src/arm/64/loopfilter.S; that file retains the upstream copyright and
BSD-2-Clause identifier.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. libwebrtc (Chromium WebRTC AV1 RTP behavior)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream:   https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src
Pinned ref: refs/branch-heads/7778_178 (Chrome Stable Mac 148.0.7778.179)
Pinned at:  third_party/upstream/webrtc/ (sync via `make sync-upstreams`)
License:    BSD 3-Clause + Additional IP Rights Grant (see upstream
            https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/refs/heads/main/LICENSE
            and PATENTS in the upstream project root).

libwebrtc is consulted as a reference for AV1 RTP payload and
depayload behavior (modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_av1.cc and
its companions). No source code is copied verbatim from libwebrtc
into this repository; the influence on the RTP packetization and
assembly code is acknowledged here.

